# The builder stage does `COPY . .`, so anything listed here would otherwise be
# baked into a cached image layer. `.env` holds live API keys: even though the
# runtime stage never copies it, the builder layer persists in local and remote
# layer caches and is readable with `docker history`.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

.git
.github
node_modules
.next
*.db
*.db-*

# Recorded vendor responses and generated site output: large, regenerable, and
# not needed to build the image.
fixtures
fixture-site
docs
mockups
tests
*.md
!README.md
